<title>UK: Cable &amp; Wireless up after HK telecom report.</title>
<headline>Cable &amp; Wireless up after HK telecom report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cable &amp; Wireless rose in early trade on Monday, echoing gains in Hong Kong Telecom after a report that C&amp;W would cut its stake in its HK unit in return for better access to the Chinese telecommunications market.</p>
<p>C&amp;W shares were up 6-1/2p at 483-1/2 by 0809 GMT.  </p>
<p>The stock was also boosted by a report in the Wall Street Journal that C&amp;W was in talks with Global One, an alliance between Sprint Corp., France Telecom and Deutsche Telecom about widespread international cooperation.</p>
</text>
